{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And enmity.</b> It is יְשׁוּפְךָ רֹאשׁ. Her seed יְשׁוּפְךָ רֹאשׁ, and likewise אֲשֶׁר בְּשַׂעֲרָה יְשׁוּפֵנִי (Job 9:17), for the bet is not seen in the scriptural text after it, and the bet is missing as in the bet found in בֵּית ד׳ (2 Kings 12:17)." "<b>Heel.</b> It is the foot. And if the head is first, this is last, and likewise וְאֵת עֲקֵבוֹ מַיִם (Joshua 5:13)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "Resolved the abbreviated verse citation מ״ב as 2 Kings (Melakhim Bet); the idiom involves the bet of בית being absent/not seen, referring to the form ישופך where a prefixed bet may have dropped.", 1 "The Joshua citation reads in full 'ואת עקבו מים'; the fragmentary quotation is preserved as Ibn Ezra gives it."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:04.246336417Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}